    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1015">

                <pb facs="1264" n="1246" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24523/9–246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cooper</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-04T18:00:00-04:00">September 4, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>769. Embtel 954 Sept. 2. Confirming Amb’s tel conversation today with Braden you
                    should inform Pres his proposal not found practicable by Dept for following
                    reasons: (1) actual judicial cooperation not effective since only Peruvian court
                    would hear all witnesses; (2) under US military law written police statements
                    inadmissible as evidence; (3) in court martial accused would have no opportunity
                    interrogate or cross examine Peruvian witnesses. Further for your own confid inf
                    acquittals by US court followed by Peruvian convictions might expose former to
                    ridicule and in any event unfavorable publicity might result here on question of
                    double jeopardy.</p>
                <p>You should accordingly comply Dept’s 756 Aug 28 acceding to Peruvian Govt’s
                    position re jurisdiction after seeking assurances outlined and expressing this
                    Govt’s trust quick and speedy justice will be meted as well to all Peruvian
                    citizens involved regrettable incident. Please cable text note submitted.</p>
                <p>War Dept advised of above and is taking steps for immediate return Perú of Pvt
                    Borli.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
